#{[{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116097} :activity/id #uuid "f5bf1856-47b4-5455-be99-90d735981501" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116097 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116486 :tutorial/content "We have already seen some properties of matrix multiplication. For example, multiplying any $n \\times n$ square matrix $A$ by the identity matrix $I_n$ will leave it unchanged:\n\n$$\nA I_n = I_n A = A.\n$$\n\nAlso, matrix multiplication follows the **distributive laws**:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(A+B)C & =AC+BC, \\\\ C(A+B) & =CA+CB.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "60b5c83f-3d84-5140-80c7-c4640bea28b0" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2997 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "0b9aabff-e92b-5507-9327-e103c1c53a12" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116098}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116098 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea"} :step/id #uuid "5f6895fd-de2c-5b1d-96fd-486f6bcbc9a7" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116099}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116099 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116487 :tutorial/content "If $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ are three matrices that are conformable for multiplication, then they follow the **associative law**:\n\n$$\n\\left( AB\\right) C = A\\left( BC\\right)\n$$\n\nSo, when we wish to compute a product $ABC,$ we don't always have to start by multiplying $AB.$ Alternatively, we can start by multiplying $BC,$ and then multiply $A$ by the result. \n\nSometimes rearranging the parentheses might make the computations slightly easier." :tutorial/id #uuid "31c195bb-9066-55bf-ae02-9de81da2b7bb" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2998 :tutorial/title "The Associative Law for Matrix Multiplication"} :step/id #uuid "e49acfe6-644b-55a4-86c6-154201b20646" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116100}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116100 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115227 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8feeacff-b07d-5f98-a765-4d8571674a7a"} :step/id #uuid "31661944-ebfa-574b-9783-47e41b70b808" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116119}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116101 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115228 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5a870c4a-daa5-5df2-8968-d8bf9ac0bd75"} :step/id #uuid "375c5e0d-680a-5465-afbc-b89498f3e772"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116119 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116492 :tutorial/content "In general, matrix multiplication is **not** commutative. In other words, given two general matrices $A$ and $B$ that are conformable for multiplication, we have\n\n$$\nAB \\neq BA.\n$$\n\nHowever, some particular matrices may satisfy this property. For instance, $AI = IA$ (where $I$ is the identity matrix)." :tutorial/id #uuid "4e92439e-2fc7-59ca-beb8-2ace6a7d3e71" :tutorial/math-academy-id 3129 :tutorial/title "Matrix Multiplication Is Not Commutative in General"} :step/id #uuid "c85ef919-914b-57cc-ab1b-19cb7cd36e6e" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186116101}}] :activity/title "Properties of Matrix Multiplication" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186115470}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050122 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115226 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115056 :question/id #uuid "32bd6b27-e95d-5de4-941f-309eb0bc61f1" :question/math-academy-id "e-4411" :question/problem "Find $AB-CB,$ where\n![](images/b4/b4b5ccc4e5075ba81dc840743f0267ba2e5f28d75a5be09de54df111203b949a.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB-CB=(A-C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A-C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A-C & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 7\\end{bmatrix}-\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 4 & -3 \\\\ -1 & -4 & 3 \\\\ -2 & 0 & 8\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB-CB & =(A-C)B \\\\  & =-{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & 45 \\\\ -81 & \\sqrt{5} & 2 \\\\ -2 & -1 & -\\sqrt{3}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a7ad52ce-d408-5390-b91f-c855274f39ea" :knowledge-point/question-generator {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186535153 :question-generator/id #uuid "323ae9ad-2881-54b6-834d-36e0dff79793" :question-generator/script "generate/scratch/17592186115226.py"} :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115829 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9607e1e7-f8ac-53de-9908-c1f571a0116f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -\\sqrt{3} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{5} & -\\sqrt{6} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{7} & -\\sqrt{2} & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113912} {:answer/id #uuid "a6768771-f5b7-548e-999b-f6902415943b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113913} {:answer/id #uuid "3fb0f0a6-006f-5c75-b1b8-e221a96e83b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113914} {:answer/id #uuid "44d07522-65f1-56fb-9042-731bbe25d2a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\sqrt{3} & 2 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{5} & 2\\sqrt{6} & 2 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{7} & 2\\sqrt{2} & 2\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113915} {:answer/id #uuid "7d1284d9-c607-5679-ad2a-4ed9873a1875" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113916}] :answer-field/id #uuid "80098924-46d2-51df-aebc-a0350ae533b3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113911}] :question/id #uuid "9796bb85-e5f6-55ad-ade8-918ae279a8e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-42004" :question/problem "Calculate $BA + BC$, where\n$A = \\begin{bmatrix}4 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 2 & -5 & 3 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}, B = \\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}, C = \\begin{bmatrix}-4 & -2 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 5 & -3 \\\\ 3 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115836 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13773284-d540-59d5-9332-97c84b837ffe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484855} {:answer/id #uuid "a397a770-fb84-5803-b445-bb962f0edcc9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-\\sqrt{2} & -1 & -\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -1 & -\\sqrt{5} & -1 \\\\ -\\sqrt{7} & -1 & -\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485172} {:answer/id #uuid "bd233e28-d1ff-5b24-a20c-c4ce4f8e0913" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485224} {:answer/id #uuid "ca909ceb-d495-5fda-9394-cd7bfc79f6cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485248} {:answer/id #uuid "d61c9def-9523-5682-a82f-7beb698de51e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485266}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186485248} :answer-field/id #uuid "5acf797e-8560-5305-87b5-ad22ffde0a24" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186113953}] :question/id #uuid "008d2c2b-6bdc-5e16-92ee-368e3b3e4390" :question/math-academy-id "q-42263" :question/problem "Find $AB+CB$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 10 & 11\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & 1 & \\sqrt{3} \\\\ 1 & \\sqrt{5} & 1 \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & 1 & \\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nAB+CB=(A+C)B.\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}3 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 1 & -5 & -1 \\\\ -9 & 10 & 11\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-5 & -2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 9 & -10 & -13\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+CB & =(A+C)B \\\\  & =-2{I}_{3}B \\\\  & =-2B \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-2\\sqrt{2} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{3} \\\\ -2 & -2\\sqrt{5} & -2 \\\\ -2\\sqrt{7} & -2 & -2\\sqrt{2}\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186235392 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "83e8b5b8-2dc6-502f-9895-61592963799f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234745}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234745} :answer-field/id #uuid "73f19ed8-00ca-518c-b9b0-9aa8b5d98ca5" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235100} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e3d714a7-0082-5d4f-ab9a-17597b16c336" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234904}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234904} :answer-field/id #uuid "8eddebdf-1405-58bc-9c0f-2eb87f83aa52" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235144} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c56147c9-f2b7-5667-be10-7a59be78f3d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234854}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234854} :answer-field/id #uuid "d733dbe9-c554-5e94-95f1-066ae833b632" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235234} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "dd65aedc-568a-52b0-80dd-3058db6f72f6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234893}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186234893} :answer-field/id #uuid "f602e10d-959a-555e-a86b-ac99268e9349" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186235267}] :question/id #uuid "27a916f2-ae5e-57d0-a97a-ec9cecb80707" :question/math-academy-id "q-138783" :question/problem "$$\nX+Y=\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\,Z=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nConsider the matrices above. Knowing that the matrix representation $T=\\begin{bmatrix}{t}_{11} & {t}_{12} \\\\ {t}_{21} & {t}_{22}\\end{bmatrix}$ of a linear transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=XZ+YZ,\n$$\n\nfind the values ${t}_{ij}.$\n\n                            \n                                    \n                                        \n                                            \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{11}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-1}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{12}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-2}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                                \n\n                                                \n\n                                        \n                                        \n                                        \n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        ${t}_{21}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-3}}                \n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                                        \n                                        \n$\\,{t}_{22}=$\n\n                                    \n                                \n                                    \n                            \n                                        {{field-4}}" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nXZ+YZ=(X+Y)Z.\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =XZ+YZ \\\\  & =(X+Y)Z \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ -1 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}-3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265870 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "306bf8f6-3b52-5e8e-b8bc-cbf0383e7c3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}\\sqrt{2} & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ 8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263411} {:answer/id #uuid "458d11a2-6e17-5d80-975f-41aca8028006" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186263611} {:answer/id #uuid "d85b3cd4-d405-5203-9c74-8cd0c5576888" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186264886} {:answer/id #uuid "e95305ac-6317-500c-b13b-c4fa54f18250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265028} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a751b3-c8e2-5d94-aaac-e1a351e5be6b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265176}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265176} :answer-field/id #uuid "aa1b1ce2-5868-5037-ac84-e98cacb5642f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186265550}] :question/id #uuid "940563cc-cba6-55cd-9e9b-4c5f6961f3e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-130269" :question/problem "Calculate $BA+BC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can apply the distributive law\n\n$$\nBA+BC=B(A+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $A+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -2 & 3 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 2\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 3 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 2 & -3 \\\\ 5 & -1 & -2\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}BA+BC & =B(A+C) \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}8 & \\sqrt{3} & \\sqrt{7} \\\\ \\sqrt{5} & \\sqrt{6} & \\sqrt{2} \\\\ \\sqrt{7} & \\sqrt{2} & 1\\end{bmatrix}\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "274faa62-4b23-54e2-ac7e-f2924e7c23d9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186290794} :answer-field/id #uuid "7cb19be5-4f4f-5fa0-a4c4-7913e344efe3" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292124} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "93e87f28-94c9-5988-b696-19c20bdb9dab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291270}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "0" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291270} :answer-field/id #uuid "b0da4143-5297-5b70-86e3-2956d34435fa" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292283} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb645714-2a42-5a0a-8871-a4b6b95039fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291698}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186291698} :answer-field/id #uuid "b3bf1c8f-05e1-534c-a5f6-a9092084607f" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292289}] :question/id #uuid "ebd8942f-54d2-577f-b680-a6f2a8658e9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-275515" :question/problem "Calculate $AB+AC$, where\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix}.\n$$\n\n|  |  | $4$ | $3$ | {{field-1}} |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $AB+AC=\\,\\,$ |  | {{field-2}} | $0$ | $-2$ |  |\n|  |  | $-1$ | {{field-3}} | $5$ |  |" :question/worked-solution "We apply the distributive law \n\n$$\nAB+AC=A(B+C).\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $B+C$ first:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}B+C & =\\begin{bmatrix}2 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -1 \\\\ 4 & -3 & 5\\end{bmatrix}+\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 1 \\\\ -4 & 3 & -4\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & ={I}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB+AC & =A(B+C) \\\\  & =A{I}_{3} \\\\  & =A \\\\  & =\\begin{bmatrix}4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 2 & 5\\end{bmatrix}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186292859 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b078db42-ad93-5fd2-9dbb-b3b4553a9c0c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-8" :db/id #edb/ref 17