aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ k & -4\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & 10 \\\\ k & 12\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271990 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1aee602c-4d2a-536f-b5a1-43a412811ff2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464072} {:answer/id #uuid "13c7384c-1cfa-57cc-8a50-9bf3eab8a9e2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464073}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464072} :answer-field/id #uuid "7c3b7373-e5a8-5e2b-8acc-0be10c9b59f2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464970} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "550ef764-b469-5976-ae9d-0020002e1ead" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464074} {:answer/id #uuid "d1697d54-6fd0-5d05-b11b-25f7ce8acc26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464075}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464075} :answer-field/id #uuid "1f5b3e10-e84c-56fd-8992-d584ea10b2ad" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464971} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fab9ce83-630e-5c19-ae07-249274247140" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464076} {:answer/id #uuid "7bc5ed4c-a4d9-52b6-ad58-1348db969598" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464077}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464076} :answer-field/id #uuid "5b13ee4f-81c8-5307-88d8-1a4665b341de" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464972}] :question/id #uuid "09aa5cfb-0ccb-582a-bfa8-b6151a1b73a2" :question/math-academy-id "q-139979" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,3⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}kx+3y &=1 \\\\ 7x-2y &=8.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $-3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|=3|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 3 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 3|\\begin{aligned}k & 3 \\\\ 7 & -2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 1 \\\\ 7 & 8\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186271991 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8504eb0f-93c6-5d20-8195-88dbad00b315" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464078} {:answer/id #uuid "c70ffc2d-dbef-5e28-8e5a-6e4a97b209b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464079}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464078} :answer-field/id #uuid "83c98712-e70e-5484-9096-216f3da1b3f6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464973} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "855711cd-7b19-555c-ab6e-e3cbe95bee72" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464080} {:answer/id #uuid "8f8516b4-64ce-53f5-938e-8dfecd51f520" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464081}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464080} :answer-field/id #uuid "acfad26a-36f9-5d0e-a1e7-36cd998ca21e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464974} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "988ccea1-2f9c-50fe-b323-1720447bfb02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464082} {:answer/id #uuid "725b0b06-d3c5-567b-9157-156746df62ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464083}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464083} :answer-field/id #uuid "535c6a07-6be3-5ec1-a653-291a4880438d" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186464975}] :question/id #uuid "ddc658b6-e0a7-590f-af72-c80671fc917f" :question/math-academy-id "q-139980" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}15x+8y &=-1 \\\\ kx+13y &=-31.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|$\n- **III.** $-2|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -2|\\begin{aligned}15 & 8 \\\\ k & 13\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}15 & -1 \\\\ k & -31\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329673 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "be7744ec-227d-555c-b802-95392ec513c1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467518} {:answer/id #uuid "f886a11b-86a7-5b5a-8f76-6da328b63714" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467519}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467519} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d7c76e-d109-5769-8668-62038090a469" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468480} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "86b1e6c3-5e63-57c4-9a2c-3c91c2d3c235" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467520} {:answer/id #uuid "0e0f888e-4bbc-5ac8-806d-7f7a885bfed4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467521}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467520} :answer-field/id #uuid "14df28d2-7f17-512c-aa78-54fedf4382f1" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468481} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d8c2352-983b-5658-8df2-16e409639b55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467522} {:answer/id #uuid "a3313dd9-a767-59cb-bba4-c976f1f2ec54" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467523}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467522} :answer-field/id #uuid "1283c815-0425-57c4-8ea5-2495c255615f" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468482}] :question/id #uuid "cc386e74-2622-5d48-a383-9789d25d9007" :question/math-academy-id "q-42613" :question/problem "Let $⟨-4,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}9x+11y &=-14 \\\\ 6x-ky &=-34.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=-4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 1 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n- **III.** $-4|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -4 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ -4|\\begin{aligned}9 & 11 \\\\ 6 & -k\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}-14 & 11 \\\\ -34 & -k\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186329702 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35563308-1bf5-5412-b3ac-38e945d6435f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467548} {:answer/id #uuid "8cce9941-e08e-5b25-878b-8a3e1fd19b85" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467549}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467548} :answer-field/id #uuid "14870e3e-adcd-5e31-8d98-7270ab6e02ba" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468495} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02c55623-fcd2-5073-8bbe-89c8cd4a2e52" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467550} {:answer/id #uuid "79d4acc9-9024-588c-a500-b68af6d2d348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467551}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467550} :answer-field/id #uuid "fa0e6660-67a9-5431-b123-e8f58681f385" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468496} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c20d9fe-a802-5cb2-97e5-b29befe6b81d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467552} {:answer/id #uuid "99913413-aa5b-526c-8205-7d8f2623301b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467553}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467553} :answer-field/id #uuid "7d0e47a0-8744-5d99-932d-e825a9175d73" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468497}] :question/id #uuid "854132a3-b7f0-5d3e-b0d4-55e43fe2b0f3" :question/math-academy-id "q-42984" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x+5y &=k \\\\ 2x-y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-13$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=-1$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|=13$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 5 \\\\ 2 & -1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =-3-10 \\\\  & -13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}|}{-13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =(-1)(-13) \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}k & 5 \\\\ -4 & -1\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186338767 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8ae2925c-3b96-520c-a0d3-abd31d1b1a7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467800} {:answer/id #uuid "a8c35df2-2bc6-5aff-a8c0-5983afd08cee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467801}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467800} :answer-field/id #uuid "9964608f-6d33-5d23-ad89-67c51daca483" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468621} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f51e75d4-d650-5dde-bab9-f44d9ed0ba19" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467802} {:answer/id #uuid "2ddc6cc2-a2f6-5c31-89bf-5e97f4160d3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467803}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467802} :answer-field/id #uuid "21a74bb3-8d72-54f1-aaee-8348f893cc5c" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468622} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "554d0d1b-860a-576b-b335-77efc0624d21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467804} {:answer/id #uuid "4374345d-6d8f-5041-923b-26fb3a674b3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186467805} :answer-field/id #uuid "b1ccbcc4-dfe8-569e-8534-c9a02b85e5b8" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468623}] :question/id #uuid "e21820bb-bc15-5fe3-a578-6f44daf46f1f" :question/math-academy-id "q-70252" :question/problem "Let $⟨-1,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}2x+ky &=-4 \\\\ 3x-4y &=5.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-2|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n- **III.** $|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|=-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}2 & k \\\\ 3 & -4\\end{aligned}| & =-|\\begin{aligned}-4 & k \\\\ 5 & -4\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345293 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c7a2c945-cc7a-516f-b667-0d89251d3b88" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468196} {:answer/id #uuid "40dd3909-7386-578c-83fe-14ada120188c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468197}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468197} :answer-field/id #uuid "a689391a-097b-5af2-9f28-47cb333ebeda" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468819} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd7b34da-0847-5b45-af70-c9c06b31eade" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468198} {:answer/id #uuid "a7025902-02fe-5c8c-8871-b5a8b672cf56" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468199}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468198} :answer-field/id #uuid "55fe37fb-e330-5dc6-9f1e-3cb5a382485e" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468820} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9f36311c-d5c2-569b-97ab-eaf35ae46749" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468200} {:answer/id #uuid "4903bf3a-5ec0-502a-9315-987f705aa1f8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468201}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468200} :answer-field/id #uuid "efa69594-ec70-57b1-b89f-3696a43adfec" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468821}] :question/id #uuid "dfe3c702-6424-5bb5-8a56-52b5a6e22724" :question/math-academy-id "q-77400" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,-2⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=k\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-6$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n- **III.** $|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|=3$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1+2 \\\\  & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ -2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|}{3} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}| & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186345294 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d68061f9-26f7-5cb1-b451-9613d07f582b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468202} {:answer/id #uuid "305d62c3-fb2c-554a-888b-993e673cc358" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468203}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468202} :answer-field/id #uuid "7204a3ea-ab6b-5c40-bbe8-ec855216acb2" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468822} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29506dd5-d859-5ad5-9d4b-430345bd390d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468204} {:answer/id #uuid "8aa20fab-5c90-5c84-a527-307ae07a2504" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468205}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468204} :answer-field/id #uuid "5ae3e59d-3a9b-58cd-9548-f87659ec9274" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468823} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "db9a7f34-a705-56e4-95cf-26717aba6aa0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468206} {:answer/id #uuid "b87a5642-b55a-55d3-b69c-559ebce5dc2b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468207}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468207} :answer-field/id #uuid "f473da0d-0013-52fe-bd69-e5c67cc3e1ac" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186468824}] :question/id #uuid "a75a54e5-59f0-5536-9005-ac12974e1a69" :question/math-academy-id "q-77401" :question/problem "Let $⟨x,1⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}3x-y &=k \\\\ x+4y &=3\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n- **I.** $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=5$\n- **II.** $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=-7$\n- **III.** $|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|=13$\n\nSelect all that apply." :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =12+1 \\\\  & =13.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $y$ is given by $y=\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{y} & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}1 & =\\frac{{D}_{y}}{D} \\\\ 1 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}|}{13} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}3 & k \\\\ 1 & 3\\end{aligned}| & =13\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"III only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441147 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "13abba68-c603-520c-b95e-bae74246f467" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441124} {:answer/id #uuid "37e0bd1c-a3ae-5f52-a82d-3a71181d02f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441127} {:answer/id #uuid "45f349a4-8a10-5b19-b4f8-85a49af13560" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441129} {:answer/id #uuid "8d3a2a97-810a-5f83-ae72-fc21a76e36d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441132} {:answer/id #uuid "ed90928a-c1d1-55de-ac12-d5f61d39fd02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441139}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441127} :answer-field/id #uuid "1aec48af-7f8c-53fd-bb3d-101ace543e43" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441144}] :question/id #uuid "1485a2c5-d3d5-5ae7-bfda-a8f34f74aef0" :question/math-academy-id "q-77402" :question/problem "Let $⟨2,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}4x+ky &=5 \\\\ x+2y &=-4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nII. $2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|=2|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ 2 & =\\frac{|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|}{|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ 2|\\begin{aligned}4 & k \\\\ 1 & 2\\end{aligned}| & =|\\begin{aligned}5 & k \\\\ -4 & 2\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441149 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1f13ed83-8c4f-597b-9f02-b31307021e5b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441126} {:answer/id #uuid "3cc8305b-aa26-5938-bd09-82bace4ba090" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441128} {:answer/id #uuid "742473cb-daf1-51d3-8173-d6d820c2cd4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441131} {:answer/id #uuid "bd29ef89-365b-598b-abba-79648038c1f5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441134} {:answer/id #uuid "f4490cc5-d61d-513b-835c-43fda69e74cc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441141}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441134} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb7f776c-eb99-528b-aabd-b4033c71b940" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441146}] :question/id #uuid "9a324339-2131-569e-b62b-73969b420199" :question/math-academy-id "q-42985" :question/problem "Let $⟨-12,y⟩$ be the solution of the system of equations below. \n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}7x+9y &=42 \\\\ kx+10y &=-4.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nWhich of the following equations could be solved to find the value of $k?$\n\nI. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-12$\n\nII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=-38$\n\nIII. $|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|=456$" :question/worked-solution "The determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAccording to Cramer's rule, the value of $x$ is given by $x=\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D},$ where\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}42 & 9 \\\\ -4 & 10\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =420+36 \\\\  & =456.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{{D}_{x}}{D} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{456}{|\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}|} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =\\frac{456}{-12} \\\\ |\\begin{aligned}7 & 9 \\\\ k & 10\\end{aligned}| & =-38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"II only\"."}] :knowledge-point/title "Solving for a Coefficient in a 2x2 Linear System Using Cramer's Rule"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119844 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119658 :question/id #uuid "d81e32a1-bd93-5a95-bb4a-e8df9063b5aa" :question/math-academy-id "e-5230" :question/problem "Consider the system of linear equations\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \nAccording to Cramer's rule, the unknown $x$ can be written as\n![](images/f5/f5c9b1c83ed648b56b47bd370ba5b15359521492087eda769d4122be99384a0f.svg)\nExpress $D_x$ in terms of a $2 \\times 2$ determinant." :question/worked-solution "We are given the system\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x-y &=2 \\\\ 2x+y &=1.\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\n \n\nThe determinant of the coefficient matrix is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to construct $D_x$, we replace the first column of the coefficient matrix by the right-hand side column of the given system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{D}_{x} & =|\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}|\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e7580024-f357-57d4-94f2-85c25e2c144b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120446 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "d2abd408-06c0-5adc-8063-ba068837455e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 10 \\\\ -2 & 8\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118791} {:answer/id #uuid "d7ea6662-5b54-5d4a-8af4-3b000fa7ad1d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118792} {:answer/id #uuid "28f8b67f-33f0-5bb5-b585-a7536d4da250" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}10 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118793} {:answer/id #uuid "6ce2b231-481f-5745-b4a6-c16fba068cc5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}8 & -2 \\\\ 10 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118794} {:answer/id #uuid "764c498a-271b-5760-aa7c-2df8b6f46e8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{vmatrix}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118795}] :answer-field/id #uuid "e9c2179b-8d21-5ea2-9af5-5d84d8a70979" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186118790} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d07e982-b1c1-5995-9925-9e692e804131" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}7 & 1 \\\\ -2 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392536} {:answer/id #uuid "0ee851b3-b898-50b2-9196-a4874185704e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}10 & -2 \\\\ 8 & 1\\end{aligned}|" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186392537} {:answer/id #uuid "83828304-8136-5f51-93d4-275dd25f6fcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "|\\begin{aligned}1 