d #edb/ref 17592186559948 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402256 :question/id #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1"} :step/id #uuid "85bcb97e-37af-5ca8-9d58-81d4ae0c6fbe" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559913}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559959 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304971 :question/id #uuid "c249fd8c-dcff-5201-89e1-bb6d2a206072"} :step/id #uuid "ae8d1bdd-e6e6-5260-8dba-9c55868390df" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559904}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559974 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559813 :question/id #uuid "63cc57b7-1fbb-5327-9f12-ff47fb613fec"} :step/id #uuid "d89e8710-7753-5df9-a5a6-86101a7dcce9"}] :activity/title "The Intersection Between a Line and a Plane" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/review} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559005}] :db/id #edb/ref 17592186050148 :topic/knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119836 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119650 :question/id #uuid "1d809050-9477-5de6-8c95-7294804e7b69" :question/math-academy-id "e-4943" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5,3,-4 \\rangle + t \\langle 4,-2,-3 \\rangle, \\qquad \t\\Pi: \\mathbf{r} \\cdot \\langle -7,5,1 \\rangle = -65.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 5+4t , 3-2t, -4-3t \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-2t,-4-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-7,5,1⟩ & =-65 \\\\ -7(5+4t)+5(3-2t)+(-4-3t) & =-65 \\\\ -35-28t+15-10t-4-3t & =-65 \\\\ -41t & =-41 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5+4(1),3-2(1),-4-3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨9,1,-7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(9 , 1, -7).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "abef3da6-252e-51e4-b816-9ef7233b9a5d" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120226 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9884d5e8-c0d4-5eb6-9188-a7a52f27eb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117518} {:answer/id #uuid "266afbbe-3a5e-5405-b0ca-02646080f267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442963} {:answer/id #uuid "676389da-d8bf-5b92-bcd7-a398a98b3965" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442966} {:answer/id #uuid "c7bcd1a1-4127-5759-8dbc-c749468c35cb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442972} {:answer/id #uuid "cfddec79-fecc-5697-9dc1-640959c5e5fc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e4728cad-b3da-5e14-bea1-edda7db46313" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117517}] :question/id #uuid "d936aa91-f337-5522-833b-6e328b8ac933" :question/math-academy-id "q-33068" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,1⟩+t⟨2,2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩=4.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =4 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,2t,1+t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-1,4⟩ & =4 \\\\ 2(3+2t)-2t+4(1+t) & =4 \\\\ 6+4t-2t+4+4t & =4 \\\\ 6t & =-6 \\\\ t & =-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(-1),2(-1),1+(-1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,-2,0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,-2,0).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120238 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ca840ec-b85c-5a60-b621-da025cc5a2c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3, 9,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117588} {:answer/id #uuid "cce176cd-cebd-5e12-82ca-1e280b2c1b6d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9, 7, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117589} {:answer/id #uuid "1fe74ec6-3551-50ea-bb3a-499c1c479388" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3, 7,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117590} {:answer/id #uuid "504f5a9e-4005-50b3-a4c6-02c750c397ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117591} {:answer/id #uuid "7d85cc60-42fa-5cfd-9c82-003bf01155f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2, 2, 3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117592}] :answer-field/id #uuid "40fd6241-2f5a-58a4-bb31-53c1cc5cf8e8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186117587}] :question/id #uuid "e7e86a35-4377-5c38-b579-c81b34ecf9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-33202" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n$l: r = ⟨0, 4, 6⟩ + t⟨1,-1, 5⟩, Π: r \\cdot ⟨ - 2, 2, 3⟩ =-7$."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244119 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "294ba218-1daa-5810-8c0f-2f6acd8c75c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241541} {:answer/id #uuid "80ad0a1e-1756-5a49-9b2f-9d4b9ef60109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242308} {:answer/id #uuid "aadff1e9-6c7e-5d09-9506-053838a505c9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-8,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242675} {:answer/id #uuid "b2007fe7-22ad-59da-993e-722977c6ff8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242730} {:answer/id #uuid "b6a1cf24-acb8-5308-bd66-0a248ae9151a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242780}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242308} :answer-field/id #uuid "f7869c8b-6cef-5966-84f9-fe7d762f95d8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243870}] :question/id #uuid "96c2dbc6-8bc6-5fb7-8e78-32cd42df2601" :question/math-academy-id "q-108311" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,-2,3⟩+t⟨0,3,-1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩=-7.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ ⟨5,-2+3t,3-t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,3,-2⟩ & =-7 \\\\ 5+3(-2+3t)+(-2)(3-t) & =-7 \\\\ 5-6+9t-6+2t & =-7 \\\\ 11t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5,-2+3(0),3-0⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,-2,3⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,-2,3).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244120 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "33346643-5a69-5079-9e87-e71b323e2bb6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241631} {:answer/id #uuid "bc9c2dee-8dd9-55db-9e6b-1c482eeb61a1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242834} {:answer/id #uuid "ccead01f-468d-5f1c-902d-078e4a9ee7ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242984} {:answer/id #uuid "d702494d-1b74-5d5c-9ab3-0705b95558ca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,2,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243086} {:answer/id #uuid "e215d1bf-4af1-5c43-80f6-a7453e0a2b2c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243187}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,4,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241631} :answer-field/id #uuid "cafe1f3c-9702-5f60-b6cb-d288c6dbab10" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243794}] :question/id #uuid "14540267-d662-5ba9-9bd7-2ba100d932e1" :question/math-academy-id "q-108313" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-1⟩+t⟨5,-2,4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩=22.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,-2t,-1+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨0,1,-2⟩ & =22 \\\\ 0(3+5t)+1(-2t)+(-2)(-1+4t) & =22 \\\\ -2t+2-8t & =22 \\\\ -10t & =20 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-2),-2(-2),-1+4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,4,-9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-7,4,-9).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314881 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0eb8f532-8109-56ef-8ea6-7d7e8fda174e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,31,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312080} {:answer/id #uuid "30de8d47-2f26-5381-bc67-4eb0ee992123" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312369} {:answer/id #uuid "a7f8512a-48d0-5872-a500-e1de657bfe34" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,13,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313291} {:answer/id #uuid "e2b9d8a5-8b12-541b-b956-720a78e83b1b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313762} {:answer/id #uuid "f5cde894-634d-5f97-9e4d-09a5ae155357" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,-20,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313942}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-20,13,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312369} :answer-field/id #uuid "85681f3e-c4a0-5f09-ab05-6853a3e1d4ae" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314365}] :question/id #uuid "f60e171f-8d34-5a7f-bcb5-85d2254301da" :question/math-academy-id "q-33988" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+t⟨-5,2,7⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩=30.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ ⟨5-5t,3+2t,-4+7t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,3,1⟩ & =30 \\\\ 2(5-5t)+3(3+2t)-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 10-10t+9+6t-4+7t & =30 \\\\ 3t & =15 \\\\ t & =5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨5-5(5),3+2(5),-4+7(5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-20,13,31⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-20,13,31).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2280cb71-d56d-5c11-9ffc-9e7ac8621681" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-17,-10,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339424} {:answer/id #uuid "51d70f39-09be-5fe0-b06a-f48d5b7f85d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339879} {:answer/id #uuid "7923bb17-a47c-5f0f-aa70-02c9163dfd5d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340209} {:answer/id #uuid "a3365d47-2432-5573-a0bc-2a03360f17ae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340608} {:answer/id #uuid "ed6d6aad-b4fa-596f-8dd5-f5bc35997084" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-10,-13,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341222}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,-10,17)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340209} :answer-field/id #uuid "0ab4e761-07dd-58e8-b46a-0567acd50ed3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341400}] :question/id #uuid "b7b7455d-19c2-5862-8ffa-6bf81d08e53f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73985" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨3,2,-3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩=6.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ ⟨2+3t,2t,2-3t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,-2,3⟩ & =6 \\\\ 5(2+3t)-2(2t)+3(2-3t) & =6 \\\\ 10+15t-4t+6-9t & =6 \\\\ 2t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-5.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-5$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+3(-5),2(-5),2-3(-5)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-13,-10,17⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-13,-10,17).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342125 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "25a8eacf-acaa-535b-84fd-68dd0e55e537" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,-3,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339449} {:answer/id #uuid "9245627b-7ed9-5a81-a591-0bddaf5c1488" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340440} {:answer/id #uuid "95647350-28b0-50f0-ba88-074ca618981c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340476} {:answer/id #uuid "a8076978-e0f4-543d-834d-5fa159290d6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340652} {:answer/id #uuid "cce78ef0-b9c9-5c65-96ff-bcf9b11be57b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340943}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-3,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340652} :answer-field/id #uuid "75a90e21-4110-5920-b29a-9528326a3c34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341586}] :question/id #uuid "a27e98ee-3a96-559d-b75b-2bf4d0ce11d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-73987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,1,1⟩+t⟨5,2,-4⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩=36.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ ⟨1+5t,1+2t,1-4t⟩\\cdot ⟨2,-3,5⟩ & =36 \\\\ 2(1+5t)-3(1+2t)+5(1-4t) & =36 \\\\ 2+10t-3-6t+5-20t & =36 \\\\ -16t & =32 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+5(-2),1+2(-2),1-4(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-9,-3,9⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-9,-3,9).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399608 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01df1bcb-4a7b-5150-ad54-aeccce8f3856" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399610} {:answer/id #uuid "38c936a1-d976-513a-81ce-1b234231b7aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399611} {:answer/id #uuid "039d4336-0a52-5143-9cf6-0afb00570546" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,7,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399612} {:answer/id #uuid "663befe7-68ee-5370-a09d-addae6ba4a9d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399613} {:answer/id #uuid "012c8472-6cf0-52d5-b45e-45eeef9775df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399614}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,5,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399610} :answer-field/id #uuid "44bd467d-d957-573d-927f-7c7473314928" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399609}] :question/id #uuid "310a805e-d3a4-5eae-9540-0ee13a3dc212" :question/math-academy-id "q-108309" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,-1⟩+t⟨-1,2,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩=11.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨2-t,3+2t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,1,4⟩ & =11 \\\\ -2(2-t)+1(3+2t)+4(-1+3t) & =11 \\\\ -4+2t+3+2t-4+12t & =11 \\\\ 16t & =16 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=1$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-1,3+2(1),-1+3(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,5,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(1,5,2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399615 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "05af7225-4beb-5fce-9b53-b954446029e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399617} {:answer/id #uuid "8eed67c2-0aa3-5e76-b961-1c7f471f1326" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,3,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399618} {:answer/id #uuid "0c95b6c8-08a8-5564-b42b-eddd5578aa82" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399619} {:answer/id #uuid "b4bbb97f-13d1-5230-847b-f5130e3b18df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399620} {:answer/id #uuid "631fd696-26bf-5859-a6c1-43ab338d85a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,7,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399621}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,7,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399621} :answer-field/id #uuid "0dbc9dfe-4ec5-5030-8d6e-d34195de294f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399616}] :question/id #uuid "8e5fe668-3628-59a7-b261-da619f1e8497" :question/math-academy-id "q-108310" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,3,0⟩+t⟨3,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩=-19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,3-2t,t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,1,-3⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)+1(3-2t)-3t & =-19 \\\\ -8+12t+3-2t-3t & =-19 \\\\ 7t & =-14 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=-2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(-2),3-2(-2),(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-8,7,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(-8,7,-2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186403738 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7d6e560d-c0f9-5b00-9374-501b77816db3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403740} {:answer/id #uuid "0d5dad58-6f17-557a-a47c-3daedf8cd066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-6,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403741} {:answer/id #uuid "697db66d-1d20-570e-bd42-19a3bff15801" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403742} {:answer/id #uuid "2a612b0e-faeb-5123-a818-5a85e0cc7103" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403743} {:answer/id #uuid "f4069451-0a02-5138-bd42-c9a8964d8236" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,2,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403744}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403742} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8a46fca-92cb-569e-aaa5-ff42267626c0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186403739}] :question/id #uuid "36894dd9-ad4f-58c5-8fd6-dfd9706bcecb" :question/math-academy-id "q-73984" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,2,7⟩+t⟨-5,-6,0⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩=-24.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ ⟨3-5t,2-6t,7⟩\\cdot ⟨-6,5,4⟩ & =-24 \\\\ -6(3-5t)+5(2-6t)+4\\cdot 7 & =-24 \\\\ -18+30t+10-30t+28 & =-24 \\\\ 20 & =-24.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442983 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8834e13a-22fa-5aac-a999-328918db52aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442967} {:answer/id #uuid "96d49a2f-474b-5bba-b6c4-17e8726cbd43" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442968} {:answer/id #uuid "b83d1b54-86e9-5e63-af2b-8d6d7fdb32d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,2,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442970} {:answer/id #uuid "f64b86a2-04c6-5e9a-9cf2-346fe66c641a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,2,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442976} {:answer/id #uuid "fa261700-7670-52be-9dc1-2ffc7832aa15" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442978}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,2,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442967} :answer-field/id #uuid "c7e90ddb-8e9f-5cb4-bec1-a99d63f38772" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442981}] :question/id #uuid "8e5d0c94-6cbf-5053-b8da-ce1333f1257b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108308" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,2,1⟩+t⟨3,0,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩=13.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ ⟨-1+3t,2,1+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,-1,2⟩ & =13 \\\\ 1(-1+3t)-2+2(1+2t) & =13 \\\\ -1+3t-2+2+4t & =13 \\\\ 7t & =14 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=2$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+3(2),2,1+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,2,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5,2,5).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442984 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00128b0b-75f1-5ff4-8a3e-54c15cf052dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442960} {:answer/id #uuid "0db1cb8d-ae91-58aa-ba6d-996ec7b29ea2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442961} {:answer/id #uuid "25dfd479-4874-55fc-ac79-5aafbe7a30f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442962} {:answer/id #uuid "66855eaf-d25e-59dd-8568-e9296afde634" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442965} {:answer/id #uuid "bc96ece3-ea6d-5cb5-94a3-9ae65aed87a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-5,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442971}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442962} :answer-field/id #uuid "3a04dab5-4de0-5a23-bb85-4c890b9f023c" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442979}] :question/id #uuid "a985335b-cba4-5e25-b462-ecfeb2395155" :question/math-academy-id "q-108315" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-3,4⟩+t⟨4,-2,1⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩=1.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ ⟨1+4t,-3-2t,4+t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,-3,2⟩ & =1 \\\\ -2(1+4t)+(-3)(-3-2t)+2\\cdot (4+t) & =1 \\\\ -2-8t+9+6t+8+2t & =1 \\\\ 15 & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "4220dbdf-b64e-566f-ae49-56f619b94daf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475539} {:answer/id #uuid "a263b19c-dab2-51ad-a37c-4d7d02bba31d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475682} {:answer/id #uuid "b1727d54-c85a-57b8-a08b-528c454ea97c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475704} {:answer/id #uuid "b314dcbd-c630-5e14-8975-1aa386fad831" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475708} {:answer/id #uuid "ea3afca3-5485-5e1f-b70b-ffd448191cf1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475802}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475539} :answer-field/id #uuid "49aa9793-d791-5a4c-9561-114186e2e854" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475854}] :question/id #uuid "6079a48b-0752-583a-8f2a-84194653fec2" :question/math-academy-id "q-33972" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,4,-1⟩+t⟨1,4,3⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩=45.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩ & =45 \\\\ ⟨2+t,4+4t,-1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,12,9⟩ & =45 \\\\ 3(2+t)+12(4+4t)+9(-1+3t) & =45 \\\\ 6+3t+48+48t-9+27t & =45 \\\\ 78t & =0 \\\\ t & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$ is obtained by substituting $t=0$ into the equation of the line, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(0),4+4(0),-1+3(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2,4,-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(2,4,-1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475947 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "10f49541-bf17-51d7-9f75-37616f1a6089" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-1,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475468} {:answer/id #uuid "60c57a2e-889c-5474-81d3-a55d65fdd34b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,2,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475585} {:answer/id #uuid "813ea0c8-6a02-5346-b587-75a643aadca7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,4,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475635} {:answer/id #uuid "b4214275-5327-55f6-a028-7523f95b454a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475710} {:answer/id #uuid "bbf64d63-9b14-5d35-91c0-7a22161af6ec" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475730}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475730} :answer-field/id #uuid "1cedb4ab-8127-56c0-a22d-80bf5a1ac4a8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475837}] :question/id #uuid "8ef5750d-a5da-50af-8419-8b1661dfe47b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108319" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-2⟩+t⟨3,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩=8.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ ⟨5-3t,3-t,-2+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,5⟩ & =8 \\\\ -2(5+3t)+4(3-t)+5\\cdot (-2+2t) & =8 \\\\ -10-6t+12-4t-10+10t & =8 \\\\ -8 & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559858 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40fa63da-8d25-5d94-97fe-f363984d351a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-24,4,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559182} {:answer/id #uuid "54bfb8e5-1bc3-55dc-b6bb-ca377e8ee977" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559232} {:answer/id #uuid "a0e9bf2c-81b2-536b-98ec-2dd8b4e53ea4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559423} {:answer/id #uuid "abe12585-4813-5617-a74b-afa58fdb9f12" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559447} {:answer/id #uuid "b300f230-78be-5357-879b-21a0f3bf43a5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,6,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559462}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559232} :answer-field/id #uuid "fff9c6a5-d7fa-5ed1-9590-bb662eb6e249" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559771}] :question/id #uuid "c9dd16b9-4054-5136-a332-5517b98207e0" :question/math-academy-id "q-33977" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨4,1,6⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩,\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩=-32.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's write the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨4+2t,1+6t,6⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨4+2t,1+6t,6⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =-32 \\\\ ⟨4+2t,1+6t,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =-32 \\\\ -24(4+2t)+8(1+6t)+6\\cdot 6 & =-32 \\\\ -96-48t+8+48t+36 & =-32 \\\\ -52 & =-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Vector Form and a Plane in Dot Product Form"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119837 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119651 :question/id #uuid "c1576b30-9142-5884-b654-7ade7a765ec7" :question/math-academy-id "e-4944" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n\n$$\nl: \\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1,3,1 \\rangle + t \\langle 2,1,0 \\rangle, \\qquad  \\Pi:4x-3y+2z-7 = 0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle .\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x-3y+2z-7 & =0 \\\\ 4x-3y+2z & =7 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $\\mathbf{r} = \\langle 1+2t , 3+t, 1 \\rangle$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,3+t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,2⟩ & =7 \\\\ 4(1+2t)-3(3+t)+2\\cdot 1 & =7 \\\\ 4+8t-9-3t+2 & =7 \\\\ 5t & =10 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),3+(2),1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,5,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(5 , 5, 1).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120229 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "153f3c4f-9bb4-575a-bf5e-88b04e29d58a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302595} {:answer/id #uuid "75ca0ec4-f115-5eaf-8978-84b0e49468fa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303175} {:answer/id #uuid "a800de77-92dc-5141-bd29-c54cd12e4e51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491} {:answer/id #uuid "cd43b129-2b04-51da-afc7-ea0b002f1f58" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,7,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303723} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b25123-f5a5-5705-961f-c56f3f92d28c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-2,19)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303973}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,0,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303491} :answer-field/id #uuid "aba170b3-1e35-5d70-ae58-276390f33698" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304545}] :question/id #uuid "a9c8b702-f6a3-5488-9345-1b22f3aeec01" :question/math-academy-id "q-33081" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-1}{2}=\\frac{y+2}{1}=\\frac{z-1}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩=19.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(1,-2,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨2,1,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨1,-2,1⟩+t⟨2,1,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+2t,-2+t,1+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,6,2⟩ & =19 \\\\ (1+2t)+6(-2+t)+2(1+3t) & =19 \\\\ 1+2t-12+6t+2+6t & =19 \\\\ 14t & =28 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨1+2(2),-2+2,1+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨5,0,7⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(5,0,7).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120239 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6d74ada3-9243-5f7c-ade2-62caa4b9c021" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,1,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402088} {:answer/id #uuid "2ddeb712-2499-5385-8cf5-8d5841c638be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402089} {:answer/id #uuid "c3a42789-8ed3-50da-bd89-5ed82656d5bd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402090} {:answer/id #uuid "4f5b4306-4e52-5f8f-a6c5-d9a8c474f65b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402091} {:answer/id #uuid "b73612ac-9159-5b03-82b8-04dc3dbeb325" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402092}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402092} :answer-field/id #uuid "1ba93ced-d091-5536-afc3-ce47413fdf3f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402087}] :question/id #uuid "49e4fa98-401d-5c2d-a49c-1997a8550033" :question/math-academy-id "q-33203" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-5,0,1⟩+t⟨-3,1,0⟩,\\,Π:-3x+y-2z+27=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+y-2z+27 & =0 \\\\ -3x+y-2z & =-27 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ ⟨-5-3t,t,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,1,-2⟩ & =-27 \\\\ -3(-5-3t)+1\\cdot t-2\\cdot 1 & =-27 \\\\ 15+9t+t-2 & =-27 \\\\ 10t & =-40 \\\\ t & =-4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-4$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-5-3(-4),-4,1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,-4,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,-4,1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244184 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "534563ab-ad8a-52e8-ab28-8e3cb647e59b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241926} {:answer/id #uuid "7a481cbd-1cba-520f-9744-7029c9f2825f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242254} {:answer/id #uuid "8328eaca-6d43-51d5-944b-f122a23c3edb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,4,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242325} {:answer/id #uuid "9c702dd4-0c20-5809-9cb3-7a9d9423cb1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242545} {:answer/id #uuid "d5b52c46-df5f-5397-a641-365480e0da3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,8,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243071}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,4,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242254} :answer-field/id #uuid "62df7e56-3c54-5d7e-9fb7-92c76ce4e2dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243629}] :question/id #uuid "7ed76edb-2aee-5101-83be-e4a973b64993" :question/math-academy-id "q-108891" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{1-z}{2},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩=-9.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,4,-2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,0,1⟩+t⟨3,4,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304962 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01d22185-31e1-5c2b-95d2-848598ea1898" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,0,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302463} {:answer/id #uuid "60c4e451-1a44-53d9-a6db-f9fb648545be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,-2,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303045} {:answer/id #uuid "67e0400e-fa7a-57ba-96e7-b214d9574656" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-5,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303086} {:answer/id #uuid "a7d1ed36-c9fa-51a0-96ce-45e0b3571939" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303488} {:answer/id #uuid "dcb202fe-418e-5930-8986-b2659604d5eb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303834}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,-5,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303488} :answer-field/id #uuid "7dc757d8-b74c-5e82-84ca-760fef027983" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304415}] :question/id #uuid "8c9e4b1e-64e1-5274-81d9-5dc1e69f7cbb" :question/math-academy-id "q-33194" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,1,0⟩+t⟨1,3,2⟩,\\,Π:3x-2y+4z+6=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+4z+6 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+4z & =-6 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ ⟨2+t,1+3t,2t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,4⟩ & =-6 \\\\ 3(2+t)-2(1+3t)+4(2t) & =-6 \\\\ 6+3t-2-6t+8t & =-6 \\\\ 5t & =-10 \\\\ t & =-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2+(-2),1+3(-2),2(-2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,-5,-4⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(0,-5,-4).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304967 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2e6df193-b69e-5d2f-b044-5daa7b2c6fd3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-1,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302743} {:answer/id #uuid "37f463ed-451f-59a2-b374-c8de1c1a8c48" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186302800} {:answer/id #uuid "76daa4dd-d618-5b12-b5b4-48a9a6d2a605" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303187} {:answer/id #uuid "84336cc7-b3e1-55ed-9aff-f6416c09cc9e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,-3,-11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303280} {:answer/id #uuid "9be8eb89-3f6c-5504-8645-77c912d4ca38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303424}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303187} :answer-field/id #uuid "96a48539-cc4e-5984-a08e-0d56ef7c55ec" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304480}] :question/id #uuid "00b27684-fae1-56d0-a859-d1fc21cc59df" :question/math-academy-id "q-33197" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-2}{-3}=\\frac{y-3}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{-1},\\,Π:3x-2y+z-38=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(2,3,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨-3,2,-1⟩.$ Therefore, its parametric equations are given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨2,3,-4⟩+t⟨-3,2,-1⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+z-38 & =0 \\\\ 3x-2y+z & =38 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ ⟨2-3t,3+2t,-4-t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-2,1⟩ & =38 \\\\ 3(2-3t)-2(3+2t)+(-4-t) & =38 \\\\ 6-9t-6-4t-4-t & =38 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨2-3(-3),3+2(-3),-4-(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨11,-3,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(11,-3,-1).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186304971 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9ccad579-7ffd-5028-82c9-8be517c44ccf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303432} {:answer/id #uuid "c5a96f69-83dc-57ab-88b1-de0764e272b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,2,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303669} {:answer/id #uuid "dc88a9e0-a58d-507d-8dbf-f29575569623" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303833} {:answer/id #uuid "f8782171-7da4-599e-a483-393f0200a20e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,8,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304012} {:answer/id #uuid "f9f6c3e0-0705-5423-bdeb-301d579540f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304023}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,8,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186303432} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0993881-1ebc-59b3-9c71-cbd4dfde3c44" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186304507}] :question/id #uuid "c249fd8c-dcff-5201-89e1-bb6d2a206072" :question/math-academy-id "q-33201" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,0,-4⟩+t⟨2,4,3⟩,\\,Π:4x+3y+4z-60=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+4z-60 & =0 \\\\ 4x+3y+4z & =60 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ ⟨3+2t,4t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,3,4⟩ & =60 \\\\ 4(3+2t)+3(4t)+4(-4+3t) & =60 \\\\ 12+8t+12t-16+12t & =60 \\\\ 32t & =64 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+2(2),4(2),-4+3(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨7,8,2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(7,8,2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186314820 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3ff6a580-92b7-5851-bcce-fe10c30be1cd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-2,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312490} {:answer/id #uuid "947ae6d9-2a5b-5525-86d2-6a8dcbc0bb2f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313166} {:answer/id #uuid "ae867fd0-223f-5656-84a8-6dd4a2746db7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313338} {:answer/id #uuid "bc7ae479-5f79-5a12-800f-dfc0be27aceb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-19,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313445} {:answer/id #uuid "ed86fa34-154a-507c-ade7-f09ae536f0b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313871}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-19,-5,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313445} :answer-field/id #uuid "919b5cd2-ecf2-59dc-9064-6e6d909d482b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314402}] :question/id #uuid "5873c215-84fe-562e-9b4f-b99d76cb6e63" :question/math-academy-id "q-33968" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-12,10,6⟩+s⟨1,0,4⟩+t⟨2,6,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,4⟩\\times ⟨2,6,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 6 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 4 \\\\ 6 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 4 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 6\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-24i+8j+6k \\\\  & =⟨-24,8,6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =⟨-12,10,6⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,3,2⟩+w⟨-5,-2,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ ⟨1-5w,3-2w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨-24,8,6⟩ & =404 \\\\ -24(1-5w)+8(3-2w)+6(2-w) & =404 \\\\ -24+120w+24-16w+12-6w & =404 \\\\ 98w & =392 \\\\ w & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=4$ into the vector equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1-5(4),3-2(4),2-(4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-19,-5,-2⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-19,-5,-2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342129 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e017315-e476-5fa0-8361-dc00652a6489" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,0,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340405} {:answer/id #uuid "ad64653c-387b-56c4-988a-77711f82ccae" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340706} {:answer/id #uuid "af463bcf-e431-5d1e-a420-7660e1b98031" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-5,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340726} {:answer/id #uuid "d8153fa3-e604-533d-b56e-b26114f3d4d7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341045} {:answer/id #uuid "f86bd550-c5e7-5c4a-ad94-8436818324a3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341326}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341045} :answer-field/id #uuid "9343b686-98f1-53b8-a0c6-e7d798a3b52a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341638}] :question/id #uuid "156769fc-4325-56fe-a6f3-a488d1baa118" :question/math-academy-id "q-74004" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-5,4,2⟩+s⟨0,3,1⟩+t⟨2,0,1⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨0,3,1⟩\\times ⟨2,0,1⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 0 & 3 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}0 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 0\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =3i+2j-6k \\\\  & =⟨3,2,-6⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =⟨-5,4,2⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3,1,5⟩+w⟨-2,-5,4⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ ⟨3-2w,1-5w,5+4w⟩\\cdot ⟨3,2,-6⟩ & =-19 \\\\ 3(3-2w)+2(1-5w)-6(5+4w) & =-19 \\\\ 9-6w+2-10w-30-24w & =-19 \\\\ -40w & =0 \\\\ w & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=0$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨3-2(0),1-5(0),5+4(0)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,1,5⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(3,1,5).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399636 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0dd2ac48-7620-52cc-95be-704f08884c59" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-3,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399638} {:answer/id #uuid "bdec2734-53b3-5679-b71d-75f8bcbc08d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399639} {:answer/id #uuid "546f5e56-43c2-5956-b6c9-0175baee1711" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399640} {:answer/id #uuid "65add1a9-10b0-59ed-9c8d-f16bb33c3988" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,0,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399641} {:answer/id #uuid "25644b17-ee2a-5eb9-ae20-64906545cc37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(14,-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399642}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(14,-4,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399642} :answer-field/id #uuid "1e560f3d-0487-5833-a63c-2ddd954cbbe7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399637}] :question/id #uuid "0da8771f-0983-5e77-be97-afe167de38df" :question/math-academy-id "q-108371" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨10,-5,12⟩+s⟨4,3,0⟩+t⟨0,2,5⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vector to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨4,3,0⟩\\times ⟨0,2,5⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 4 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 5\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}3 & 0 \\\\ 2 & 5\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 5\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}4 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =15i-20j+8k \\\\  & =⟨15,-20,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =⟨10,-5,12⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨4,-2,3⟩+w⟨5,-1,2⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ ⟨4+5w,-2-w,3+2w⟩\\cdot ⟨15,-20,8⟩ & =346 \\\\ 15(4+5w)-20(-2-w)+8(3+2w) & =346 \\\\ 60+75w+40+20w+24+16w & =346 \\\\ 111w & =222 \\\\ w & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨4+5(2),-2-(2),3+2(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨14,-4,7⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(14,-4,7).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399650 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c181d54f-7b5e-5e40-b660-5db606239a3a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,7,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399652} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2c2f01-60e6-5197-ae47-76dd272575a0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,3,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399653} {:answer/id #uuid "100fc206-faa0-5c9a-8c1d-f828c27459ba" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399654} {:answer/id #uuid "a03ac96b-8e87-5579-959e-6059ecf3486c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399655} {:answer/id #uuid "d6d8eeca-91ef-5d44-a9a1-da7d1707ffce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399656}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-12,-5,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399654} :answer-field/id #uuid "3cd4a0b3-55ce-54d3-98c8-8b7021d46e30" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399651}] :question/id #uuid "2d225520-d7e9-5a28-afbf-6e16563a3611" :question/math-academy-id "q-108889" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x-3}{5}=\\frac{y-1}{2}=\\frac{z+4}{3},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩=39.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(3,1,-4)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨5,2,3⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨3,1,-4⟩+t⟨5,2,3⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ ⟨3+5t,1+2t,-4+3t⟩\\cdot ⟨-3,2,-1⟩ & =39 \\\\ (-3)(3+5t)+2(1+2t)-(-4+3t) & =39 \\\\ -9-15t+2+4t+4-3t & =39 \\\\ -14t & =42 \\\\ t & =-3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=-3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨3+5(-3),1+2(-3),-4+3(-3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-12,-5,-13⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(-12,-5,-13).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402093 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb5e385e-d48b-552d-92db-b2c42b730f55" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,8,14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402095} {:answer/id #uuid "2cec0929-bdd8-5d7b-8ece-52cdde4c6f93" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402096} {:answer/id #uuid "c23c18d5-4a2a-5884-8422-592e07e7f5b2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402097} {:answer/id #uuid "50770341-c200-5dd2-a57c-f88a32fa60ee" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,4,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402098} {:answer/id #uuid "b695496a-1b9b-5846-a379-f0e3c0d96851" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(14,8,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402099}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,8,14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402095} :answer-field/id #uuid "0878a66a-d92b-5043-a146-6c379d55810e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402094}] :question/id #uuid "eaab1f60-24fb-5572-8cfb-474f418bf09f" :question/math-academy-id "q-33205" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-1,-2,6⟩+t⟨2,5,4⟩,\\,Π:x+2y+z-33=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+2y+z-33 & =0 \\\\ x+2y+z & =33 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ ⟨-1+2t,-2+5t,6+4t⟩\\cdot ⟨1,2,1⟩ & =33 \\\\ -1+2t+2(-2+5t)+6+4t & =33 \\\\ -1+2t-4+10t+6+4t & =33 \\\\ 16t & =32 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-1+2(2),-2+5(2),6+4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3,8,14⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the intersection point is $P(3,8,14).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186402256 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee24fdf4-e1ee-5f88-bc78-1cd69107c3af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402258} {:answer/id #uuid "3cff9213-8332-5106-9a38-96d7ec4a4378" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,5,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402259} {:answer/id #uuid "9d7ebdfb-49aa-56f4-a0ad-f4d48aa68b14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402260} {:answer/id #uuid "6adfa3c5-c5cd-56cd-841d-1fd0fc016077" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402261} {:answer/id #uuid "cd22fb61-25ce-5f17-bad1-fbd4ce2f0694" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402262}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402262} :answer-field/id #uuid "f9e05243-350c-5a1d-ad1e-5c71c37318cb" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186402257}] :question/id #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442982 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "613bfe5f-02e2-5735-9f79-164b162ce348" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-1,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442964} {:answer/id #uuid "a6b4a532-3b78-5ed1-a6e7-746b7ec7ab3f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-3,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442969} {:answer/id #uuid "d748dd3f-d487-5117-bef8-07f995fa3631" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,3,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442974} {:answer/id #uuid "de970a68-1f18-57df-a82c-3fb7858ebc0a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,5,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442975} {:answer/id #uuid "f85e9e92-164c-5dbe-a1e2-300ee4897290" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442977}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442977} :answer-field/id #uuid "817f92e5-c306-5bc0-98bb-5216ce23f4dd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442980}] :question/id #uuid "2968eff5-6f3b-5cf4-97d0-686663582eb3" :question/math-academy-id "q-108369" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨-2,1,4⟩+t⟨3,2,-6⟩,\\,Π:-4x+3y-z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-4x+3y-z-11 & =0 \\\\ -4x+3y-z & =11 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,1+2t,4-6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-4,3,-1⟩ & =11 \\\\ -4(-2+3t)+3(1+2t)-(4-6t) & =11 \\\\ 8-12t+3+6t-4+6t & =11 \\\\ 7 & =11.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475912 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "007d69dc-a2ca-580f-b0f7-74cbcfa1ebdd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475444} {:answer/id #uuid "3a25e529-3954-5987-92eb-d533381cc44b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} {:answer/id #uuid "52af092c-e727-5f18-8ff7-345347fe6d51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-8,-13,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475562} {:answer/id #uuid "572842f6-cb5d-5a22-b2c9-50266f22eb6a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475570} {:answer/id #uuid "fca47535-789f-5b0b-98b2-271a04ca1b25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-14,-21,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475823}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,31,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475523} :answer-field/id #uuid "d8937436-576e-5320-a137-6b981c96167e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475895}] :question/id #uuid "07e33caa-9650-5834-8d9a-46cc82f723d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-108434" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨5,3,-4⟩+s⟨1,0,2⟩+t⟨0,-2,3⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨1,0,2⟩\\times ⟨0,-2,3⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ -2 & 3\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =4i-3j-2k \\\\  & =⟨4,-3,-2⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =⟨5,3,-4⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨1,-1,2⟩+w⟨3,4,-1⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ ⟨1+3w,-1+4w,2-w⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,-2⟩ & =19 \\\\ 4(1+3w)-3(-1+4w)-2(2-w) & =19 \\\\ 4+12w+3-12w-4+2w & =19 \\\\ 2w & =16 \\\\ w & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=8$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨1+3(8),-1+4(8),2-8⟩ \\\\  & =⟨25,31,-6⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(25,31,-6).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475933 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00592e29-c51c-505e-aa00-3ff92195a878" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,12,-13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475443} {:answer/id #uuid "11e5504e-d64d-5f8c-ac38-3eff267389dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(25,-12,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475471} {:answer/id #uuid "d9c8c1d7-fdbb-512c-ae27-1e5f390a0545" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,-6,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475772} {:answer/id #uuid "de8b2779-f353-540b-b6dc-5741e2b54f02" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475782} {:answer/id #uuid "ec08f7ca-621a-5fb1-a281-a7c103129688" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475805}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475782} :answer-field/id #uuid "4edf1a48-e584-5a56-97e2-8850121c1df9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475855}] :question/id #uuid "42cfce4b-bf3d-5d7e-8fad-15e0c813875c" :question/math-academy-id "q-108370" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨5,3,-7⟩+t⟨4,-3,2⟩,\\,Π:5x+2y-7z-15=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x+2y-7z-15 & =0 \\\\ 5x+2y-7z & =15 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ ⟨5+4t,3-3t,-7+2t⟩\\cdot ⟨5,2,-7⟩ & =15 \\\\ 5(5+4t)+2(3-3t)-7(-7+2t) & =15 \\\\ 25+20t+6-6t+49-14t & =15 \\\\ 80 & =15.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect."} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475975 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "35e34ef5-0c0f-566b-94a8-9376d485a3d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,0,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475516} {:answer/id #uuid "384678c4-4350-5113-9f0f-32d8e2cf6110" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,1,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475518} {:answer/id #uuid "92098877-886b-53fa-a483-755c30d71d2e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,3,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475660} {:answer/id #uuid "b2c22028-564a-5c89-ab16-c9763fcf688a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475706} {:answer/id #uuid "c36ccfc7-634d-5201-b479-3d9288da2e97" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475739}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-7,-3,10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475706} :answer-field/id #uuid "d9d0e6f8-2892-55f4-a237-affcef970729" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475897}] :question/id #uuid "e4fbd5e6-b819-591a-880c-a933bdaba9d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-33082" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩,\\,Π:r=⟨-15,1,1⟩+s⟨2,0,2⟩+t⟨1,4,0⟩.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of a plane in the parametric form $r=p+tv+sw$, we have that its normal vector is $n=v\\times w.$ In our case, the normal vectors to $Π$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}n & =v\\times w \\\\  & =⟨2,0,2⟩\\times ⟨1,4,0⟩ \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 2 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 4 & 0\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =|\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 \\\\ 4 & 0\\end{aligned}|i-|\\begin{aligned}2 & 2 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}|j+|\\begin{aligned}2 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}|k \\\\  & =-8i+2j+8k \\\\  & =⟨-8,2,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the equation of the plane $Π$ in dot product form is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot n & =p\\cdot n \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =⟨-15,1,1⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨2,3,1⟩+w⟨-3,-2,3⟩$ into the equation of the plane in dot product form, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ ⟨2-3w,3-2w,1+3w⟩\\cdot ⟨-8,2,8⟩ & =130 \\\\ -8(2-3w)+2(3-2w)+8(1+3w) & =130 \\\\ -16+24w+6-4w+8+24w & =130 \\\\ 44w & =132 \\\\ w & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $q$ of the intersection point $Q,$ we substitute $w=3$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}q & =⟨2-3(3),3-2(3),1+3(3)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-7,-3,10⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $Q(-7,-3,10).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186515570 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a4e4e53-6530-5d9b-ac71-88fa4a852643" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,5,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514894} {:answer/id #uuid "13d7977a-6ece-5a3d-a4d3-a046ae5ee70a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514914} {:answer/id #uuid "3e792c4b-0f89-58e4-ad54-bf65b7f20967" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515006} {:answer/id #uuid "97dcbf66-8c48-507d-96c6-a848577b2e92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-5,-3,-4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515192} {:answer/id #uuid "a9993b57-a418-5d19-be94-6b1c3a3b00c8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,5,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515229}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,3,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186514914} :answer-field/id #uuid "c8d9ffbc-23ef-519d-9512-884d3bb1903d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186515494}] :question/id #uuid "83aacc67-1785-59c3-94ae-6f65bea01fe4" :question/math-academy-id "q-108881" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y+1}{2}=\\frac{z}{4},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩=25.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,-1,0)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,2,4⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,-1,0⟩+t⟨3,2,4⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =25 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,-1+2t,4t⟩\\cdot ⟨3,-1,2⟩ & =25 \\\\ 3(-2+3t)-(-1+2t)+2(4t) & =25 \\\\ -6+9t+1-2t+8t & =25 \\\\ 15t & =30 \\\\ t & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=2$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(2),-1+2(2),4(2)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨4,3,8⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(4,3,8).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line and a Plane Given in Other Forms"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119838 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119652 :question/id #uuid "f952e670-a673-5c15-913b-c396e8885142" :question/math-academy-id "e-4945" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $\\Pi$ with equations\n![](images/64/64a3661b0699fbde542ed1709bacf569f681477a5f824f0650b07d9060b82dae.svg)" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+4y+6z+25 & =0 \\\\ 3(3-4t)+4(-1+2t)+6(2+3t)+25 & =0 \\\\ 9-12t-4+8t+12+18t+25 & =0 \\\\ 14t & =-42 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $\\mathbf{p}$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-4(-3)=15 \\\\ y &=-1+2(-3)=-7 \\\\ z &=2+3(-3)=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(15,-7,-7).$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120289 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02b63af9-4f30-589d-b300-e21c0d2d64e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,5,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186311979} {:answer/id #uuid "13841e10-37b0-50ba-bd35-1206f0534f5f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15,-13,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312113} {:answer/id #uuid "3462bc81-9265-51ee-bafa-d06de12209b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-13,16,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312398} {:answer/id #uuid "7b38872c-3e3a-5601-ae6f-2de768f51760" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312957} {:answer/id #uuid "ca885b58-2c6c-560c-a288-b5c966ed0a17" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,15,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313556}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,15,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313556} :answer-field/id #uuid "6475649e-4236-5480-a4eb-e5c922b9780a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314291}] :question/id #uuid "aeb82fb0-8960-53a5-b9a1-90d3db98fe43" :question/math-academy-id "q-33986" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4+3t \\\\ y &=3+4t \\\\ z &=-2+6t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+5y+8z=229.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y+8z & =229 \\\\ 2(4+3t)+5(3+4t)+8(-2+6t) & =229 \\\\ 8+6t+15+20t-16+48t & =229 \\\\ 74t & =222 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4+3(3)=13 \\\\ y &=3+4(3)=15 \\\\ z &=-2+6(3)=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(13,15,16).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186120290 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a523b91-b0c8-5d77-ac05-a918d500094c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-9,9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186312052} {:answer/id #uuid "82d8d2f3-12d7-5f69-9c67-b4d2db7dc5da" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313028} {:answer/id #uuid "8d14825a-42af-51a3-9f03-b6163ac5f748" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-1,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313102} {:answer/id #uuid "95ed7638-8aa8-5f1b-b639-82099d0d033c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,7,-9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313173} {:answer/id #uuid "c5ba162d-d3e7-561c-ba10-731b0f92f98b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,-9,7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186313525} :answer-field/id #uuid "0d7ba987-d1b7-522f-859e-b04e23ff46bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186314051}] :question/id #uuid "c755ffbb-8374-5c52-a967-a6387ef6da9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-33992" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-2t \\\\ y &=-1+4t \\\\ z &=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y &=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z &=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244121 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "600b8aef-da6c-5a05-9753-24914a3499d3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(9,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242041} {:answer/id #uuid "7687f722-fb74-5a86-8afb-5ba790d4f143" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242232} {:answer/id #uuid "a77e3a01-860e-5d47-a380-4a2919fe0ab4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,0,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242649} {:answer/id #uuid "b30eea27-088d-5354-8ef8-bcf626ddf460" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242738} {:answer/id #uuid "f57050d6-b5e9-5c5f-838d-d66ca290b074" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243349}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-1,5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242738} :answer-field/id #uuid "6652b296-a21e-518a-9c5b-d45f374f2267" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243639}] :question/id #uuid "7d4770f9-017d-5451-ade2-ef9bc61cba33" :question/math-academy-id "q-108323" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=7+2t \\\\ y &=3+t \\\\ z &=1-t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:x-3y+2z=12.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x-3y+2z & =12 \\\\ 1(7+2t)-3(3+t)+2(1-t) & =12 \\\\ 7+2t-9-3t+2-2t & =12 \\\\ -3t & =12 \\\\ t & =-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=7+2(-4)=-1 \\\\ y &=3+(-4)=-1 \\\\ z &=1-(-4)=5\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-1,-1,5).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0979ee26-b4dd-5ed5-9cab-237f13bab300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,-3,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241262} {:answer/id #uuid "50818f44-1865-5083-bcf9-14855607c5c2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241899} {:answer/id #uuid "8aff1c43-eaae-5c07-92ca-05a88e6a5417" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,-4,2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242409} {:answer/id #uuid "b9391f01-11c7-5c3a-9ff7-274ffb356b92" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-2,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242804} {:answer/id #uuid "c6c8e226-835f-5977-879f-0773d4b64c21" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242934}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-4,-1,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242934} :answer-field/id #uuid "e65bb2ef-90c6-598e-9157-9a8edd5838b8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243838}] :question/id #uuid "23026cc4-61f1-51ff-9518-0d934ee1dfc2" :question/math-academy-id "q-108325" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3t \\\\ y &=-3+t \\\\ z &=4+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+y-4z+45=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+y-4z+45 & =0 \\\\ 3(2-3t)+(-3+t)-4(4+2t) & =-45 \\\\ 6-9t-3+t-16-8t & =-45 \\\\ -16t & =-32 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3(2)=-4 \\\\ y &=-3+2=-1 \\\\ z &=4+2(2)=8\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-4,-1,8).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244124 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "476e5895-586f-57b1-a8e9-64b9c347e830" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,9,-5)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241826} {:answer/id #uuid "65e0041a-b33d-5596-9117-8e8c8d122a8b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242098} {:answer/id #uuid "b19a65f8-95fd-5d04-a4c0-b580feed54f4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-3,13,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242728} {:answer/id #uuid "b3bc4d15-10e0-5455-a652-8f5fec3c26f0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,-1,-10)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242748} {:answer/id #uuid "e16af936-42d1-5d0e-b45e-142ec3fb9818" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243183}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-6,15,-2)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243183} :answer-field/id #uuid "bd38d870-1520-58ab-a4ad-250e4f90b837" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243772}] :question/id #uuid "ba20f45e-ea9a-5cbd-a036-8965c362108b" :question/math-academy-id "q-108337" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=9-3t \\\\ y &=5+2t \\\\ z &=-7+t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+3y+5z-11=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+3y+5z-11 & =0 \\\\ 4(9-3t)+3(5+2t)+5(-7+t) & =11 \\\\ 36-12t+15+6t-35+5t & =11 \\\\ -t & =-5 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=9-3(5)=-6 \\\\ y &=5+2(5)=15 \\\\ z &=-7+5=-2\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(-6,15,-2).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342127 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b2ccf68-fbc4-58ea-80f0-c47a1f4e61c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339365} {:answer/id #uuid "1d364631-26c0-59a4-93c9-0842ba8027a4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(19,10,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339381} {:answer/id #uuid "2bfe2f6a-4b05-5041-9be9-ec95d41ced84" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,8,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339510} {:answer/id #uuid "90fc5ea2-94e0-5824-91af-e274368bde07" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429} {:answer/id #uuid "a5f82de1-4dec-5d15-9285-344580d1aa1f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,-1,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340633}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(18,11,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340429} :answer-field/id #uuid "3769c405-5ffb-59ea-8180-d6fbf6837b56" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341479}] :question/id #uuid "8a17e320-306c-50fa-b84b-f8cbe958e629" :question/math-academy-id "q-73993" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-5t \\\\ y &=2-3t \\\\ z &=-2-6t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:5x-2y+4z-132=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5x-2y+4z-132 & =0 \\\\ 5(3-5t)-2(2-3t)+4(-2-6t) & =132 \\\\ 15-25t-4+6t-8-24t & =132 \\\\ -43t & =129 \\\\ t & =-3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=3-5(-3)=18 \\\\ y &=2-3(-3)=11 \\\\ z &=-2-6(-3)=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(18,11,16).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186342128 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5220f57b-422e-531b-842b-1f584644f261" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186339883} {:answer/id #uuid "979f8148-7b8d-5ec3-a55e-fb37aea141d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(0,1,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340493} {:answer/id #uuid "b83d885e-e879-51ab-96e4-b43985498ef9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,-8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340786} {:answer/id #uuid "bb602b66-8066-5891-8e86-1da45546964a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340805} {:answer/id #uuid "bba3c359-7475-5f71-8622-34809c6c9b46" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,21,-14)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340809}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,12,-18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186340805} :answer-field/id #uuid "10fba32d-90d3-5858-a355-57f3ffefce29" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186341409}] :question/id #uuid "8d4d8f0f-1eab-5bd0-8f71-a26637e6257d" :question/math-academy-id "q-74003" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-t \\\\ y &=4+2t \\\\ z &=-6-3t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:4x+6y-3z-130=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4x+6y-3z-130 & =0 \\\\ 4(5-t)+6(4+2t)-3(-6-3t) & =130 \\\\ 20-4t+24+12t+18+9t & =130 \\\\ 17t & =68 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-4=1 \\\\ y &=4+2(4)=12 \\\\ z &=-6-3(4)=-18\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(1,12,-18).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399622 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1bd5231-6855-55f3-a5ec-61c58423a2bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399624} {:answer/id #uuid "3a87675b-c089-5d14-9db0-504805f8a6af" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399625} {:answer/id #uuid "02bc6063-6eef-56d8-b50b-eec9ca9b7e38" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(4,4,0)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399626} {:answer/id #uuid "b949434a-7780-5a3d-b4d8-3bbde783f79d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399627} {:answer/id #uuid "44390ca7-20ca-5d21-b624-15837dd00ca6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(8,6,-6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399628}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,1,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399624} :answer-field/id #uuid "b8515a18-0ebe-5740-9abf-0e5d9167649f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399623}] :question/id #uuid "60f0cd70-b4b4-5b35-85ba-563cceee9aad" :question/math-academy-id "q-108326" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=6+2t \\\\ y &=5+t \\\\ z &=-3-3t\\end{aligned}\\ri