"Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-t \\\\ y &=9-3t \\\\ z &=-1-6t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:-3x+2y+5z-85=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-3x+2y+5z-85 & =0 \\\\ -3(-2-t)+2(9-3t)+5(-1-6t) & =85 \\\\ 6+3t+18-6t-5-30t & =85 \\\\ -33t & =66 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-(-2)=0 \\\\ y &=9-3(-2)=15 \\\\ z &=-1-6(-2)=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(0,15,11).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475922 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b435381-c5b8-5b4f-8b01-26d7f6d1dc11" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,8,-3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475526} {:answer/id #uuid "9dd67c95-9e81-5450-afa6-4d059c19997b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-2,-13,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475676} {:answer/id #uuid "a07f003a-5a14-5c7f-89bb-286c19f2ac04" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,-10,9)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475679} {:answer/id #uuid "b66e1051-daa1-5d8a-8225-891009842666" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,14,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475718} {:answer/id #uuid "e50752da-554b-56dd-9852-e80a3543b73f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475794}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,14,-7)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475718} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f1f7c3c-b1c0-5d3b-9ccb-c5f535269a9b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475850}] :question/id #uuid "231a9d15-2430-5e82-a7fa-b3cd0ec4e91a" :question/math-academy-id "q-108336" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+t \\\\ y &=-1+3t \\\\ z &=3-2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+y-5z=63.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+y-5z & =63 \\\\ 2(2+t)+(-1+3t)-5(3-2t) & =63 \\\\ 4+2t-1+3t-15+10t & =63 \\\\ 15t & =75 \\\\ t & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2+5=7 \\\\ y &=-1+3(5)=14 \\\\ z &=3-2(5)=-7\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(7,14,-7).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475941 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "14828947-21b5-5b44-8ba4-a8c5ac78f5e1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475474} {:answer/id #uuid "1d11cddd-41a7-59cd-a0f7-eb0c9bbb8aab" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475480} {:answer/id #uuid "495e886a-52d9-5c59-8c47-3821329f3910" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17,32,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475553} {:answer/id #uuid "ab4f8ebf-675e-5768-87c1-628fdd24f267" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,2,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475693} {:answer/id #uuid "dcf5feda-7db4-5eea-9893-715ff228f6be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,12,15)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(17,32,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475553} :answer-field/id #uuid "8d36f85e-f322-5625-a3c0-402881668478" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475874}] :question/id #uuid "789a0f9b-548a-5d80-a6d7-b592e86b7749" :question/math-academy-id "q-74001" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3t \\\\ y &=-3-7t \\\\ z &=1-2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:-2x+4y-7z=17.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y-7z & =17 \\\\ -2(2-3t)+4(-3-7t)-7(1-2t) & =17 \\\\ -4+6t-12-28t-7+14t & =17 \\\\ -8t & =40 \\\\ t & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=2-3(-5)=17 \\\\ y &=-3-7(-5)=32 \\\\ z &=1-2(-5)=11\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(17,32,11).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186475955 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3d3759ca-f415-569b-a33a-acb5640cdbd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15,-17,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475527} {:answer/id #uuid "4d264b47-4019-5711-a224-f0cc582f5fc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,3,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475558} {:answer/id #uuid "95eb3494-b745-564b-b1bb-9df9395d27c5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475667} {:answer/id #uuid "c1d7c847-242b-5cf2-ae20-6f260249b5dd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(13,35,31)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475738} {:answer/id #uuid "da243a84-b978-5f29-8ece-2e8668c34cc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(5,3,3)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475773}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(15,-17,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475527} :answer-field/id #uuid "380c38bf-f532-5171-bcc5-76a194ee6084" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186475847}] :question/id #uuid "b3b4f2c0-7489-5ff6-9c21-54c57d280888" :question/math-academy-id "q-73997" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-2t \\\\ y &=8+5t \\\\ z &=-7-4t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-3y+z-94=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3y+z-94 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-3(8+5t)-7-4t & =94 \\\\ 10-4t-24-15t-7-4t & =94 \\\\ -23t & =115 \\\\ t & =-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-5$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=5-2(-5)=15 \\\\ y &=8+5(-5)=-17 \\\\ z &=-7-4(-5)=13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(15,-17,13).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186484201 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "20fc86f8-0368-54eb-a3e0-3cf6b0379332" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} {:answer/id #uuid "2143e54b-67d5-5002-957a-3bf88c230ca4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(24,-11,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483624} {:answer/id #uuid "257b548a-b52d-5b2d-8a2f-57d74b50d39c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483630} {:answer/id #uuid "7944f3e7-3b31-5e5a-b5cb-a1562208eb42" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(11,-13,11)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483813} {:answer/id #uuid "a0a4f2b9-c6e0-5e67-8ab6-66d592472d45" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(26,12,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483899}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-16,-16,13)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186483621} :answer-field/id #uuid "15f90597-4c03-5ae4-b2c2-f42eae091087" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186484091}] :question/id #uuid "12b4f5c6-720f-5c2c-b1e8-295eb7dcb29c" :question/math-academy-id "q-73991" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-2t \\\\ y &=5-3t \\\\ z &=-1+2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x-2y+6z=62.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x-2y+6z & =62 \\\\ 3(-2-2t)-2(5-3t)+6(-1+2t) & =62 \\\\ -6-6t-10+6t-6+12t & =62 \\\\ 12t & =84 \\\\ t & =7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=6$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=-2-2(7)=-16 \\\\ y &=5-3(7)=-16 \\\\ z &=-1+2(7)=13\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(-16,-16,13).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516797 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "58a61e2d-79ec-5942-a542-a599506c947f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,8,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516299} {:answer/id #uuid "5933b3cc-3b81-55f6-a9e9-d8ce70b49ee7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-4,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516303} {:answer/id #uuid "8c3399b1-2e8d-5048-9705-3b903a795275" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516404} {:answer/id #uuid "be96b637-0ffd-5d98-b663-5c2fe316eeca" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(6,-4,-16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516515} {:answer/id #uuid "f5f1cb12-78bd-54f6-9673-719b825438c6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,5,-1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516624}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(2,8,4)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516299} :answer-field/id #uuid "96cd3fdc-919f-5a7e-9267-58831d9b0de1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516725}] :question/id #uuid "47b66d2c-d386-5a47-ab3a-e7307c9bb3f9" :question/math-academy-id "q-108335" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4-t \\\\ y &=2+3t \\\\ z &=-6+5t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:6x-4y+z+16=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-4y+z+16 & =0 \\\\ 6(4-t)-4(2+3t)+(-6+5t) & =-16 \\\\ 24-6t-8-12t-6+5t & =-16 \\\\ -13t & =-26 \\\\ t & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=4-2=2 \\\\ y &=2+3(2)=8 \\\\ z &=-6+5(2)=4\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(2,8,4).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186516801 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "140b7152-7be6-5b10-b162-4dcea3796757" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(23,5,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516151} {:answer/id #uuid "7062112e-23e0-5023-abc6-42331af0e0bc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(3,50,6)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516364} {:answer/id #uuid "739dc482-cca6-5907-b91b-15164a66f7c4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(32,50,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516369} {:answer/id #uuid "cde85d08-f475-531a-bd01-73f6eb9051bb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(12,25,36)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516547} {:answer/id #uuid "d54b4cb0-06e8-5602-a1ad-89fba9fb6215" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516561}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(32,50,16)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516369} :answer-field/id #uuid "616c22d5-e3ac-50e3-88f8-ae593e1ea4d6" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186516692}] :question/id #uuid "4c18b1c7-8bdd-5391-9b67-8443fd23166f" :question/math-academy-id "q-73998" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=8+3t \\\\ y &=-6+7t \\\\ z &=2t\\end{aligned}\\right.\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+5y-8z=186.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y-8z & =186 \\\\ 2(8+3t)+5(-6+7t)-8(2t) & =186 \\\\ 16+6t-30+35t-16t & =186 \\\\ 25t & =200 \\\\ t & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=8$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\left\\{\\begin{aligned}x &=8+3(8)=32 \\\\ y &=-6+7(8)=50 \\\\ z &=2(8)=16\\end{aligned}\\right.\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(32,50,16).$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186559813 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d0857e4-1338-5c7a-ad65-1684adcb89b5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(7,-5,12)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559130} {:answer/id #uuid "2fdae745-6cbf-5dbe-bdd2-ea7547e9e300" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(10,9,1)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559139} {:answer/id #uuid "8cea1e50-21c3-5c40-9866-c7a6949c9931" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-1,6,8)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559371} {:answer/id #uuid "98765244-eaa1-58ef-9963-d3e5ae56d7ed" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,7,18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559400} {:answer/id #uuid "df482e11-da20-5e10-9235-bb050ae6ebf4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "No intersection" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559566}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(1,7,18)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559400} :answer-field/id #uuid "f4196ccd-0e24-51af-ad66-5ad460d2a7e2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186559763}] :question/id #uuid "63cc57b7-1fbb-5327-9f12-ff47fb613fec" :question/math-academy-id "q-73995" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-3+t \\\\ y=-1+2t \\\\ z=2+4t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:6x+4y+3z=88.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x+4y+3z & =88 \\\\ 6(-3+t)+4(-1+2t)+3(2+4t) & =88 \\\\ -18+6t-4+8t+6+12t & =88 \\\\ 26t & =104 \\\\ t & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=4$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}x=-3+4=1 \\\\ y=-1+2(4)=7 \\\\ z=2+4(4)=18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(1,7,18).$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Intersection Point of a Line in Parametric Form and a Plane in Cartesian Form"}] :topic/math-academy-id 1808 :topic/title "The Intersection Between a Line and a Plane"}] [{:activity/_scope [{:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101854} :activity/id #uuid "8d861dcd-02c5-53fa-858a-2be900cad05a" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101854 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101952 :tutorial/content "Suppose we are given the following matrix:\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 8 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe denote the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}3$rd row and $\\color{red}2$nd column using the notation $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}.$\n\nThe first subscript represents the row and the second subscript represents the column. So $a_{{\\color{blue}3}\\color{red}2}=8,$ as shown below.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}2 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 0 & -2 \\\\ -1 & \\boxed{8} & 1 \\\\ 0 & 3 & -7\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nWe can denote every entry of a matrix in this way.\nFor instance, $a_{{\\color{blue}4}\\color{red}1}$ denotes the entry that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}4$th row and $\\color{red}1$st column.\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & {a}_{13} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & {a}_{23} \\\\ {a}_{31} & {a}_{32} & {a}_{33} \\\\ {a}_{41} & {a}_{42} & {a}_{43}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$" :tutorial/id #uuid "34f3a63d-a273-50fb-b26a-ae172c7e93e9" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2969 :tutorial/title "Introduction"} :step/id #uuid "71c4da2c-9ba7-5b55-a1fc-62db722468f0" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101855}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101855 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100988 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "8d783281-8364-5597-a804-a4ea0d76bec8"} :step/id #uuid "557b3c46-5feb-5a02-969f-d023d0d4b18f" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101856}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101856 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100989 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ecd07ea0-767d-55f0-a61c-da49dd320f89"} :step/id #uuid "f3dc9f2c-54de-514f-806c-13cfc1cafb33" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101857}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101857 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101953 :tutorial/content "In general, we denote the entry of a matrix $A$ that lies at the intersection of the $\\color{blue}i$th row and $\\color{red}j$th column by $a_{{\\color{blue}i}\\color{red}j}.$\n\nIf $A$ is an $m\\times n$ matrix, we can write it as\n\n$$\n\\begin{bmatrix}{a}_{11} & {a}_{12} & \\cdots & {a}_{1n} \\\\ {a}_{21} & {a}_{22} & \\cdots & {a}_{2n} \\\\ \\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots \\\\ {a}_{m1} & {a}_{m2} & \\cdots & {a}_{mn}\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nwhere each entry $a_{ij}$ is defined for $i = 1,2,\\ldots,m$ and $j =1,2,\\ldots,n.$" :tutorial/id #uuid "775ac64e-8b63-5c51-824d-1d99d17a2a0a" :tutorial/math-academy-id 2970 :tutorial/title "General Form of a Matrix"} :step/id #uuid "bd3801a8-679e-5a33-b62a-575a32786880" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101858}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186101858 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186100990 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1cc70bda-40cf-5860-9a47-25f290c71041"} :step/id #uuid "456e8474-5f06-554c-9b60-c29b26039234"}] :activity/title "Index Notation for Matrices" :activity/type {:db/ident :activity.type/lesson} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186101034} {:activity/first-step {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567530} :activity/id #uuid "d275672e-6f93-4dc3-bafb-46f0625385c3" :activity/steps [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567530 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398270 :question/id #uuid "5aee8772-02f1-5e96-b1e0-f67b0c259d43"} :step/id #uuid "d338f6d0-85fb-486f-850e-fd7862664063" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567531}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567531 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269010 :question/id #uuid "0f770f62-3fda-5a7c-ad0a-d63eb715c9d0"} :step/id #uuid "dc9f5497-4932-4614-95b1-81f62c07a24c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567532}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567532 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295088 :question/id #uuid "c95438bb-9c3d-5b94-8cd7-da3897ba153e"} :step/id #uuid "0adf70dd-62fe-473e-83d2-790bfcfb006c" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567533}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567533 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186400191 :question/id #uuid "bf0cde7f-5b94-5af7-b3da-c7304b62c190"} :step/id #uuid "755448a9-b153-4a4b-9fa0-5265b9c50809" :step/next {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567534}} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186567534 :step/content {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186269009 :question/id #uuid "4e9da133-83fb-5896-92de-79cce7846abc"} :step/id #uuid "2006f931-45d8-48d4-9621-e89e6b9098d3"}] :activity/ti